 "documentation": {
  "summary": "Drink Me: taking a bottle changes a four-metre furnished room to fourfold scale in a cut, then relocates the visitor onto its food tower. Descend and compare the enlarged room exit with a doorway that kept its size.",
  "layout": "21 by 22 metre gallery. A fixed four-metre transverse wall at source row 2 joins the hall sides to the small room front, with a three-cell opening at x=9..11 around its 1.4-metre entrance. It makes the room the forward route while permitting retreat through the same entrance. The scale_me anchor at cell (10,2) builds a four by four metre room; its fourfold state occupies sixteen by sixteen metres inside this hall. The continuous museum floor remains underneath, 4 cm below the room floor. Descend the serving plates, use the enlarged far-side room door, pass the separate fixed 1.8 by 2.4 metre witness frame, then turn toward the museum exit at (10,21). The room owns its walls and ceiling; the transverse wall, witness frame and museum remain outside the multiplication.",
  "objective": "Discover how preserved proportions can change bodily access when the body is held constant."
